-- 074-diagonal: the Tier-2 masked add as a map on the whole record row. Twin of 074-diagonal.bqn. (was t2-diagonal)
-- Formal witness: the BQN sibling proves a local order or symmetry fact only; it does not classify all entity programs.
-- Sym(I) equivariance, the diagonal action: the masked add acts on the whole record row, so permuting rows commutes with it.
-- The .bqn witnesses the flagship line as W = gold + 1000×nord; its fixture has no twoHanded, so the twin adds a scaffold twoHanded column with every value 61: TwoHanded > 60 passes on all rows and the selection reduces to nord, exactly W's gate.
-- expect gold is the .bqn's hand-computed anchor W gold‿nord. The diagonal-action quantification over taus and the single-column counterexample (permuting gold alone across a nord boundary) are Sym(I) equivariance witnesses, left to the .bqn twin.
--! registry ../registries/074-diagonal.reg
--! expect gold = 1100 200 1300 1400 500

Nord & TwoHanded > 60 , Gold += 1000
